*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* IR2111 - Half-bridge driver (single input, internal dead time)
* Behavioral ("functional") macromodel for LTspice.
*
* Based on:
*   International Rectifier, "IR2111 Half-Bridge Driver", Data Sheet
*   No. PD-6.028C (Control Integrated Circuit Designers' Manual, B-39..B-45)
*
* This is NOT a transistor-level model.  Every block of the Functional Block
* Diagram is reproduced by its terminal behaviour, with the numbers taken from
* the Static and Dynamic Electrical Characteristics tables (TYPICAL column).
* The point is to simulate the gate drive of a half-bridge - one logic
* input, the internal dead time, bootstrap, UVLO - inside a closed-loop
* converter: fast, convergent and independent of the time step.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* PIN ORDER  (8-lead DIP / SO-8 pin order; pin 5 is not connected)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*   1  VCC   low-side and logic supply        6  VS   high-side floating return
*   2  IN    logic input (in phase with HO)   7  HO   high-side gate drive
*   3  COM   low-side and logic return        8  VB   high-side floating supply
*   4  LO    low-side gate drive
*
*   X1 VCC IN COM LO VS HO VB IR2111
*
*   IN high -> HO on, LO off;  IN low -> LO on, HO off  (Figure 1).
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT IS MODELLED
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  * Logic input: CMOS Schmitt trigger referred to COM, thresholds
*    proportional to VCC at the guaranteed limits of the table: rising
*    threshold VIH = 0.62*VCC + 0.2 (6.4 / 9.5 / 12.6 V at VCC = 10 / 15 /
*    20 V), falling threshold VIL = 0.45*VCC - 0.7 (3.8 / 6.05 / 8.3 V).
*    750 k pull-down (IIN+ = 20 uA at 15 V), clamp diodes to VCC and COM.
*  * Dead time: each output is turned on ton = 850 ns and off toff = 150 ns
*    after the input edge (typ, CL = 1 nF), so between one output starting to
*    fall (90 %) and the other starting to rise (10 %) there are
*    DT = ton - toff = 700 ns (Figure 5).  Both outputs use the same delay
*    chain, so the delays are matched (MT ~ 0).  The delays are linear ramps:
*    an input pulse shorter than ~ton is swallowed by the dead-time block,
*    as in the real part.
*  * UVLO on VCC (8.6 V / 8.2 V typ) and on VBS (8.4 V / 8.1 V typ), with
*    hysteresis.  VCC under-voltage holds both outputs low; VBS
*    under-voltage holds HO low.  HO only comes back on the NEXT rising edge
*    of IN after the fault clears (the high side is set by edge pulses
*    through the level shifter, so a fault resets its latch).  LO follows IN
*    again as soon as VCC is good.
*  * Output stages: pull-up and pull-down, I = Isat*tanh(V/V0)/tanh(2),
*    Isat = IO+ = 250 mA and IO- = 500 mA typ at VBIAS = 15 V, knee
*    V0 = VBIAS/2.  The gate of each output device is ramped (pre-driver),
*    which together with Isat sets tr = 80 ns and tf = 40 ns (typ, 1 nF).
*    No cross-conduction between the two output devices.  Body diodes
*    HO-VB, VS-HO, LO-VCC, COM-LO.
*  * Quiescent currents IQCC = 70 uA, IQBS = 50 uA typ at 15 V.  Gate charge
*    is drawn from VCC (LO) and from VB (HO) - the bootstrap capacitor sees
*    it.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT IS NOT MODELLED  (behavioural model - know the limits)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  * The datasheet has no curves against VCC or temperature: the delays and
*    the edges do not change with VCC.  The output current is scaled with
*    VBIAS by the same law as the IR2110 (Figures 26B/27B of its datasheet),
*    an assumption.  KD / KE scale the delays and the edges (KD = 1.2 and
*    KE = 1.6 come close to the MAX column at 25 C).
*  * No bootstrap diode inside (the IR2111 has none - put your own).
*  * Offset supply leakage (ILK <= 50 uA at 600 V), dVs/dt immunity,
*    negative VS transients and latch-up: not modelled.  The 600 V rating is
*    not policed.
*  * The input thresholds sit at the guaranteed limits (VIH min, VIL max);
*    a real part switches somewhere in between.
*  * With VCC under the UVLO the outputs are actively held low down to 0 V
*    of supply (5 % of the normal sink strength) - the real part's behaviour
*    with a fully discharged supply is not specified.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* PARAMETERS  (override per instance:  X1 ... IR2111 KD=1.2 KE=1.6)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  KD       delay factor (1 = typical, ~1.2 = max column at 25 C)
*  KE       rise/fall-time factor (1 = typical, ~1.6 = max column)
*  VIHA, VIHB   rising threshold  VIHA*VCC + VIHB          (0.62, 0.2)
*  VILA, VILB   falling threshold VILA*VCC + VILB          (0.45, -0.7)
*  RIN      input pull-down                                (750k)
*  CIN      input capacitance (not in the datasheet)       (2 pF)
*  COUT     HO / LO pin capacitance (not in the datasheet) (10 pF)
*  UVCCP/N  VCC UVLO rising / falling threshold            (8.6 / 8.2 V)
*  UVBSP/N  VBS UVLO rising / falling threshold            (8.4 / 8.1 V)
*  TON, TOFF  ton / toff, input 50 % -> output 10 % / 90 %, 1 nF, ns (850/150)
*  TER, TEF   output gate ramp, ns (fitted to tr / tf)
*  TOON, TOOF time from the start of that ramp to 10 % / 90 % of the output
*             into 1 nF, ns (fitted; subtracted from ton / toff)
*  TFAST    release time of the device that turns off, ns  (3)
*  ISU, ISD output short-circuit current, source / sink, at 15 V, A (0.25/0.5)
*  KIO      Isat change per +5 V of VBIAS (IR2110 law)    (0.42)
*  KV0      output knee as a fraction of VBIAS             (0.5)
*  IQCC, IQBS   quiescent supply currents at 15 V          (70u 50u)
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* LTspice .FRA / .AC / .OP
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* No time-dependent sources, no internal oscillator; every Schmitt trigger,
* UVLO and latch is an integrating set/reset cell with DC solutions 0 and 1
* only, and every delay or edge is a finite-slope ramp written so that its
* DC value is exact, with no kink where a node rests.  The operating point
* needs no search and the edge times move continuously with the input,
* whatever the time step.
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.SUBCKT IR2111 VCC IN COM LO VS HO VB
+ KD=1 KE=1 VIHA=0.62 VIHB=0.2 VILA=0.45 VILB=-0.7 RIN=750k CIN=2p COUT=10p
+ UVCCP=8.6 UVCCN=8.2 UVBSP=8.4 UVBSN=8.1
+ TON=850 TOFF=150 TER=27.5 TEF=13.7 TOON=33.3 TOOF=12.6 TFAST=3
+ ISU=0.25 ISD=0.5 KIO=0.42 KV0=0.5
+ IQCC=70u IQBS=50u

*==============================================================================
* SUPPLIES, UVLO
* Internal "digital" nodes are 0..1 V, referred to COM.
* Every state bit (Schmitt trigger, UVLO, latch) is an INTEGRATING
* set/reset cell, the same construction as the UC3854 and L6599A models:
*
*     C dq/dt = G * ( S*(1-q) - R*q ),   G = 1 mA/V, C = 1 pF (1 ns)
*     S = set   OR ( q > 0.5 AND NOT reset )
*     R = reset OR ( q < 0.5 AND NOT set )
*
* With neither input active the cell is parked at 0 or 1, the only DC
* solutions are 0 and 1, and it holds its state whatever the step size.
* For a Schmitt trigger, S = (input above the upper threshold) and
* R = (input below the lower one), each a 10 mV-wide linear ramp.
*==============================================================================
Bvcc  n_vcc COM V = max(0, V(VCC,COM))
Bvbs  n_vbs COM V = max(0, V(VB,VS))

* VCC UVLO (n_okc = 1: VCC good)
Bokcs n_okcs COM V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_vcc,COM)-{UVCCP})*100+0.5))
Bokcr n_okcr COM V = max(0,min(1,({UVCCN}-V(n_vcc,COM))*100+0.5))
Bokcq n_okcq COM V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_okc,COM)-0.5)*20))
Bokc  COM n_okc I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_okcs,COM), V(n_okcq,COM)*(1-V(n_okcr,COM)))*(1-V(n_okc,COM))
+   - max(V(n_okcr,COM), (1-V(n_okcq,COM))*(1-V(n_okcs,COM)))*V(n_okc,COM) )
Cokc  n_okc COM 1p
Rokcg n_okc COM 1G
* VBS UVLO (n_okb = 1: VBS good)
Bokbs n_okbs COM V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_vbs,COM)-{UVBSP})*100+0.5))
Bokbr n_okbr COM V = max(0,min(1,({UVBSN}-V(n_vbs,COM))*100+0.5))
Bokbq n_okbq COM V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_okb,COM)-0.5)*20))
Bokb  COM n_okb I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_okbs,COM), V(n_okbq,COM)*(1-V(n_okbr,COM)))*(1-V(n_okb,COM))
+   - max(V(n_okbr,COM), (1-V(n_okbq,COM))*(1-V(n_okbs,COM)))*V(n_okb,COM) )
Cokb  n_okb COM 1p
Rokbg n_okb COM 1G

* quiescent currents (shape as the IR2110, Figures 17B / 18B there)
Bqcc  VCC COM I = {IQCC}*pow(V(n_vcc,COM)/15, 1.7)
Bqbs  VB  VS  I = {IQBS}*pow(V(n_vbs,COM)/15, 1.7)

*==============================================================================
* LOGIC INPUT  IN  (Schmitt trigger referred to COM)
*   rising threshold  VIHA*VCC + VIHB,  falling threshold  VILA*VCC + VILB
*   (the falling one kept above 0.2*VCC at very low VCC)
*==============================================================================
.model DIR2111 D(IS=1e-15 RS=5 CJO=0)
Rin   IN COM {RIN}
Cin   IN COM {CIN}
Dinp  IN VCC DIR2111
Dinn  COM IN DIR2111
Bxs  n_xs COM V = max(0,min(1,(V(IN,COM)-({VIHA}*V(n_vcc,COM)+{VIHB}))*100+0.5))
Bxr  n_xr COM V = max(0,min(1,(max(0.2*V(n_vcc,COM),{VILA}*V(n_vcc,COM)+{VILB})-V(IN,COM))*100+0.5))
Bxq  n_xq COM V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_x,COM)-0.5)*20))
Bx   COM n_x I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_xs,COM), V(n_xq,COM)*(1-V(n_xr,COM)))*(1-V(n_x,COM))
+   - max(V(n_xr,COM), (1-V(n_xq,COM))*(1-V(n_xs,COM)))*V(n_x,COM) )
Cx   n_x COM 1p
Rxg  n_x COM 1G

*==============================================================================
* HIGH-SIDE LATCH
*   q = 1 blocks HO.  Set: a VCC or VBS fault.  Reset: IN low (set wins).
*   So after a fault HO returns only on the next rising edge of IN.
*==============================================================================
* OR of the two faults, written smooth (no kink at the rest state)
Bseth n_seth COM V = 1 - V(n_okc,COM)*V(n_okb,COM)
Bqhs n_qhs COM V = V(n_seth,COM)
Bqhr n_qhr COM V = (1-V(n_x,COM))*(1-V(n_seth,COM))
Bqhq n_qhq COM V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_qh,COM)-0.5)*20))
Bqh  COM n_qh I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_qhs,COM), V(n_qhq,COM)*(1-V(n_qhr,COM)))*(1-V(n_qh,COM))
+   - max(V(n_qhr,COM), (1-V(n_qhq,COM))*(1-V(n_qhs,COM)))*V(n_qh,COM) )
Cqh  n_qh COM 1p
Rqhg n_qh COM 1G

* channel commands (0..1): HO in phase with IN, LO inverted
Bch   n_ch COM V = V(n_x,COM)*(1-V(n_qh,COM))*(1-V(n_seth,COM))
Bcl   n_cl COM V = (1-V(n_x,COM))*V(n_okc,COM)

*==============================================================================
* DEAD TIME / PROPAGATION DELAY
*   Each channel's ramp node s follows its command at a finite slope, up at
*   0.5/td_on and down at 0.5/td_off [1/ns], so it crosses 0.5 exactly td
*   after the input edge:  td_on = KD*TON - KE*TOON,  td_off = KD*TOFF -
*   KE*TOOF (the output-stage share into 1 nF subtracted).  The slow turn-on
*   IS the dead time.  With a heavier load than 1 nF the output part, and so
*   ton / toff, grow.
*   Each ramp is a slew-limited follower written as  s = target - y:
*       C dy/dt = C d(target)/dt - G*slope(y)      (C from target to y)
*   so ds/dt = slope(y): full slope beyond 0.1 of error, linear inside, the
*   up and down slopes blended smoothly (tanh) through y = 0, so there is
*   no kink where the node rests.  At DC y = 0 and s = target exactly -
*   the operating point needs no search.
*==============================================================================
Bru   n_ru COM V = 0.5/max(5, {KD}*{TON} - {KE}*{TOON})
Brd   n_rd COM V = 0.5/max(5, {KD}*{TOFF} - {KE}*{TOOF})
Btsh  n_tsh COM V = V(n_ch,COM)
Cysh  n_tsh n_ysh 1p
Bysh  n_ysh COM I = 1m*(((V(n_ru,COM))+(V(n_rd,COM)))/2 + ((V(n_ru,COM))-(V(n_rd,COM)))/2*tanh(V(n_ysh,COM)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_ysh,COM)))
Rysh  n_ysh COM 1G
Bosh  n_sh COM V = V(n_tsh,COM) - V(n_ysh,COM)
Btsl  n_tsl COM V = V(n_cl,COM)
Cysl  n_tsl n_ysl 1p
Bysl  n_ysl COM I = 1m*(((V(n_ru,COM))+(V(n_rd,COM)))/2 + ((V(n_ru,COM))-(V(n_rd,COM)))/2*tanh(V(n_ysl,COM)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_ysl,COM)))
Rysl  n_ysl COM 1G
Bosl  n_slo COM V = V(n_tsl,COM) - V(n_ysl,COM)

*==============================================================================
* PRE-DRIVER (gates of the two output devices)
*   d = comparator on the delay ramp.  u drives the pull-up, p the
*   pull-down, both 0..1.  Turning on, the pull-down is released first
*   (TFAST) and then u ramps 0 -> 1 in TER ns; turning off, the pull-up is
*   released and p ramps 0 -> 1 in TEF ns.  Each device only starts once
*   the other is (almost) off: no cross-conduction.
*==============================================================================
Bdh   n_dh COM V = min(1, max(0, 50*(V(n_sh,COM)-0.5) + 0.5))
Bdl   n_dl COM V = min(1, max(0, 50*(V(n_slo,COM)-0.5) + 0.5))
Bter  n_ter COM V = {KE}*{TER}
Btef  n_tef COM V = {KE}*{TEF}
* pull-up only once the pull-down is off, and vice versa
Btuh  n_tuh COM V = V(n_dh,COM)*min(1,max(0,1.5-20*V(n_ph,COM)))
Cyuh  n_tuh n_yuh 1p
Byuh  n_yuh COM I = 1m*(((1/V(n_ter,COM))+(1/{TFAST}))/2 + ((1/V(n_ter,COM))-(1/{TFAST}))/2*tanh(V(n_yuh,COM)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_yuh,COM)))
Ryuh  n_yuh COM 1G
Bouh  n_uh COM V = V(n_tuh,COM) - V(n_yuh,COM)
Btph  n_tph COM V = (1-V(n_dh,COM))*min(1,max(0,1.5-20*V(n_uh,COM)))
Cyph  n_tph n_yph 1p
Byph  n_yph COM I = 1m*(((1/V(n_tef,COM))+(1/{TFAST}))/2 + ((1/V(n_tef,COM))-(1/{TFAST}))/2*tanh(V(n_yph,COM)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_yph,COM)))
Ryph  n_yph COM 1G
Boph  n_ph COM V = V(n_tph,COM) - V(n_yph,COM)
Btul  n_tul COM V = V(n_dl,COM)*min(1,max(0,1.5-20*V(n_pl,COM)))
Cyul  n_tul n_yul 1p
Byul  n_yul COM I = 1m*(((1/V(n_ter,COM))+(1/{TFAST}))/2 + ((1/V(n_ter,COM))-(1/{TFAST}))/2*tanh(V(n_yul,COM)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_yul,COM)))
Ryul  n_yul COM 1G
Boul  n_ul COM V = V(n_tul,COM) - V(n_yul,COM)
Btpl  n_tpl COM V = (1-V(n_dl,COM))*min(1,max(0,1.5-20*V(n_ul,COM)))
Cypl  n_tpl n_ypl 1p
Bypl  n_ypl COM I = 1m*(((1/V(n_tef,COM))+(1/{TFAST}))/2 + ((1/V(n_tef,COM))-(1/{TFAST}))/2*tanh(V(n_ypl,COM)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_ypl,COM)))
Rypl  n_ypl COM 1G
Bopl  n_pl COM V = V(n_tpl,COM) - V(n_ypl,COM)

*==============================================================================
* OUTPUT STAGES
*   I = s * Isat(VBIAS) * tanh(V/V0)/tanh(1/KV0),  V0 = KV0*VBIAS
*   Isat = IS*(1 + KIO*(VBIAS-15)/5), floor 5 % (keeps the output held low
*   with the supply collapsed).  VBIAS = VBS for HO, VCC for LO.
*==============================================================================
Bkh   n_kh COM V = max(0.05, 1 + {KIO}*(V(n_vbs,COM)-15)/5)/tanh(1/{KV0})
Bkl   n_kl COM V = max(0.05, 1 + {KIO}*(V(n_vcc,COM)-15)/5)/tanh(1/{KV0})
Bv0h  n_v0h COM V = {KV0}*max(5, V(n_vbs,COM))
Bv0l  n_v0l COM V = {KV0}*max(5, V(n_vcc,COM))

Bhu   VB HO  I = V(n_uh,COM) * {ISU}*V(n_kh,COM) * tanh(V(VB,HO)/V(n_v0h,COM))
Bhd   HO VS  I = V(n_ph,COM) * {ISD}*V(n_kh,COM) * tanh(V(HO,VS)/V(n_v0h,COM))
Chs   HO VS  {COUT}
Dhp   HO VB  DIR2111
Dhn   VS HO  DIR2111

Blu   VCC LO I = V(n_ul,COM) * {ISU}*V(n_kl,COM) * tanh(V(VCC,LO)/V(n_v0l,COM))
Bld   LO COM I = V(n_pl,COM) * {ISD}*V(n_kl,COM) * tanh(V(LO,COM)/V(n_v0l,COM))
Cls   LO COM {COUT}
Dlp   LO VCC DIR2111
Dln   COM LO DIR2111

* DC paths for the floating domain (keep .op well posed with nothing
* connected; 1 Gohm is far below the 50 uA leakage spec)
Rvs   VS  COM 1G
Rvb   VB  VS  100Meg

.ENDS IR2111
